---
import Background from '../components/Background.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import SiteHeader from '../components/SiteHeader.astro';
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

/**
 * Privacy policy for alleyadmin.app.
 *
 * MAINTENANCE: every factual claim on this page was written against what the
 * site and Worker actually do. If you change any of the following, re-read
 * this file and update it in the same PR:
 *
 *   src/lib/analytics-events.ts        which events are sent
 *   src/lib/analytics-client.ts        how events reach GA4, and the consent gate
 *   functions/api/analytics/event.ts   the fallback path and its derived identifier
 *   worker/src/index.ts                what the signup endpoint accepts and stores
 *   worker/schema.sql                  the columns described under "The waitlist"
 *   src/components/ThemeToggle.astro   the localStorage key named below
 *
 * The Zaraz cookie names and lifetimes come from the Cloudflare dashboard
 * (Zaraz > Google Analytics 4 > Cookies), not from this repository. Re-check
 * them there if the tool configuration changes.
 *
 * A privacy policy that has drifted from the code is worse than no policy.
 */

const lastUpdated = 'August 2026';
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy | Alley Admin"
  description="What Alley Admin collects, why, and how to have it removed. Plain English, no legalese."
>
  <div class="page">
    <Background />
    <SiteHeader />

    <main class="content">
      <article class="prose">
        <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p class="last-updated">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

        <p>
          Alley Admin is a product of Toastbyte Studios. This page covers the
          website at alleyadmin.app. The league management application itself is
          still in development — when it launches with accounts and league data,
          this policy will be replaced with one that covers it properly.
        </p>
        <p>
          For now the site does two things: it counts how the page is used, and
          it stores an email address if you choose to give us one. That is the
          whole of it, and the rest of this page is the detail.
        </p>

        <h2>Analytics</h2>
        <p>
          We use Google Analytics 4 to understand how the site is used. It is
          loaded through Cloudflare Zaraz, which serves the analytics script
          from alleyadmin.app rather than from a third-party domain and sends
          the data on from Cloudflare's edge.
        </p>
        <p>We send a page view, plus these five events and nothing else:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>waitlist_signup_started</strong> — you submitted the waitlist
            form.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>waitlist_signup_succeeded</strong> — the address was accepted.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>waitlist_signup_failed</strong> — it was not, along with a reason
            such as "invalid_email" or "server_error".
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>outbound_link_clicked</strong> — you followed a link away from
            the site, along with where it pointed.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>theme_toggled</strong> — you switched between the light and dark
            themes.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          <strong>Your email address is never sent to Google Analytics</strong>,
          in any form, hashed or otherwise. The signup events record that a
          signup happened and whether it worked, never who it was for.
        </p>

        <h2>Cookies</h2>
        <p>Zaraz sets two first-party cookies on alleyadmin.app:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>cfz_google-analytics_v4</strong> — the identifier and engagement
            state kept for Google Analytics. Up to one year.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>cfzs_google-analytics_v4</strong> — state for your current visit,
            such as a page view count. Deleted when you close your browser.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Both are set for alleyadmin.app alone and do not follow you to other
          sites. We also use Cloudflare Web Analytics, which counts page loads,
          sets no cookies, and keeps no client-side state.
        </p>
        <p>
          Your light/dark preference is stored in your browser under
          <strong>aa-theme</strong>, and is only written once you click the
          toggle. It never leaves your device.
        </p>

        <h2>When analytics does not load</h2>
        <p>
          If Zaraz fails to load in your browser — a blocked script, a slow
          connection — the site falls back to sending the same events from our
          own server instead. Because there is no cookie to read in that case,
          the server derives a temporary identifier by hashing your IP address,
          browser user agent, and language setting together. It is not stored,
          and it is not linked to anything else.
        </p>
        <p>
          This is a fallback and should be rare. We would rather tell you it
          exists than leave it undocumented.
        </p>

        <h2>Opting out</h2>
        <p>
          There is no in-product opt-out yet. A consent banner is planned and
          the underlying machinery is already in place, but it is not switched
          on, so analytics currently runs for everyone who visits.
        </p>
        <p>
          Until it ships, you can block analytics with a browser extension or
          your browser's tracking protection, and clearing the cookies listed
          above resets the identifier Google Analytics uses for you.
        </p>

        <h2>The waitlist</h2>
        <p>
          If you enter your email address, we store it in a Cloudflare D1
          database. We keep <strong
            >the address and the time you submitted it</strong
          >, and nothing else — no name, no IP address, no browser details.
        </p>
        <p>
          Submitting the same address twice is silently ignored rather than
          stored again. We use the address only to tell you when Alley Admin
          launches. We do not sell it, share it, or add it to any other list.
        </p>

        <h2>Hosting</h2>
        <p>
          Like any website, this one is delivered by a host — Cloudflare — which
          processes the IP address and request details of every request in order
          to serve the site and to block abuse. That happens for every visitor
          and is separate from the analytics above.
        </p>

        <h2>Who else sees this</h2>
        <p>
          We do not sell, trade, or rent your information. Cloudflare provides
          our hosting, our database, Web Analytics, and Zaraz. Google receives
          the analytics events described above; how Google uses data from sites
          like ours is explained at <a
            href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            >policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites</a
          >.
        </p>

        <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
        <p>
          Your email address stays until you ask us to remove it, or until Alley
          Admin has launched and we no longer need it. Analytics data is kept by
          Google according to the retention setting on our property, and
          Cloudflare keeps its own logs according to its policies. Neither is
          linked to your email address.
        </p>

        <h2>Getting your data removed</h2>
        <p>
          There is no account to delete. If you gave us an email address, email
          <a href="mailto:info@toastbyte.studio">info@toastbyte.studio</a> and we
          will remove it. You can also ask what we hold or ask us to correct it.
        </p>
        <p>
          One honest limitation: analytics data is not linked to your email
          address or to any account, so we cannot look up which analytics events
          were yours in order to delete them.
        </p>

        <h2>Children</h2>
        <p>
          This site is not directed at children under 13 and we do not knowingly
          collect their information. If you believe a child has given us an
          email address, contact us and we will delete it.
        </p>

        <h2>Changes</h2>
        <p>
          We will update this page when what we collect changes, and update the
          date at the top when we do.
        </p>

        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Questions about any of this go to <a
            href="mailto:info@toastbyte.studio">info@toastbyte.studio</a
          >.
        </p>
      </article>
    </main>

    <Footer />
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .page {
    position: relative;
    min-height: 100vh;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    overflow: hidden;
    background: linear-gradient(
      180deg,
      var(--color-bg) 0%,
      var(--color-bg-sunken) 100%
    );
  }

  .content {
    position: relative;
    z-index: 10;
    width: 100%;
    max-width: var(--content-width);
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: var(--space-xl) var(--space-md) var(--space-2xl);
    flex: 1;
  }

  /* Narrower than the landing page: this is a wall of text, and a measure of
     roughly 70 characters is where it stays readable. */
  .prose {
    max-width: 70ch;
    margin: 0 auto;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .prose h1 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 4vw, 2.25rem);
    font-weight: 800;
    color: var(--color-text);
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    margin: 0 0 0.375rem;
  }

  .prose h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 1.1875rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--color-text);
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    margin: var(--space-lg) 0 0.5rem;
    padding-top: var(--space-sm);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }

  .last-updated {
    color: var(--color-text-subtle);
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-md);
  }

  .prose p {
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-sm);
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }

  .prose ul {
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-sm);
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
  }

  .prose li {
    margin-bottom: 0.375rem;
  }

  .prose strong {
    color: var(--color-text);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .prose a {
    color: var(--color-primary);
    text-decoration: none;
    border-bottom: 1px solid transparent;
    transition:
      color 0.2s var(--ease),
      border-color 0.2s var(--ease);
  }

  .prose a:hover {
    color: var(--color-primary-hover);
    border-bottom-color: currentColor;
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .content {
      padding: var(--space-lg) var(--space-sm) var(--space-xl);
    }
  }
</style>
